diff --git a/NEWS b/NEWS
index b4f88d4..2ead598 100644
--- a/NEWS
+++ b/NEWS
@@ -2,6 +2,32 @@
 
 All notable changes to `hostnamed` are documented in this file, derived from the project's git history.
 
+## [0.3.0] - 2026-10-14
+
+### Changed (build / compatibility)
+- **polkit is now a hard build dependency.** The `-Dpolkit=disabled` / `polkit` feature option has been removed, along with the unused `HAVE_POLKIT` define and every `polkit_found` conditional in the meson files. Previously a build without polkit failed at `#include <polkit/polkit.h>` anyway, and without polkit nothing could authorise the Set* methods. Anyone passing `-Dpolkit=...` to `meson setup` must drop it.
+- Hostname validation (`SetHostname`, `SetStaticHostname`) is now strict RFC 1123: labels of 1-63 characters, no empty labels (`a..b`), no leading/trailing dot, and no label that starts or ends with `-`. Names that were previously accepted but are invalid under these rules are now rejected with `InvalidArgs`.
+- `GetProductUUID` now returns the 16 raw UUID bytes (as systemd-hostnamed does) instead of the 36-character ASCII string as `ay`. It returns a `NotFound` error, rather than an empty array, when the UUID is unreadable, malformed, or the all-zero / all-0xFF placeholder.
+
+### Fixed
+- Fixed bogus `PropertiesChanged` emissions: `Chassis` and `IconName` were blanked and re-set on every resync, producing duplicate dict keys and a signal on every inotify event. The effective value (machine-info, then fallbacks) is now computed first and updated once; three file touches now produce one signal instead of ten.
+- `IconName` is now derived from the effective chassis string, so `CHASSIS=laptop` in `/etc/machine-info` without an `ICON_NAME` yields `computer-laptop` rather than `computer`.
+- `DefaultHostname` is now populated (`DEFAULT_HOSTNAME` from os-release, else `localhost`); it was always empty.
+- `HostnameSource` can now report `default` (static hostname unset and kernel hostname unset, `(none)`, or equal to the default); it previously only ever reported `static` or `transient`.
+- `SetPrettyHostname` no longer truncates arbitrary labels at the first dot. The leading-label reduction now applies only when the whole value is a valid hostname, so `Bob's PC v2.0` is stored as given while `dair.example.net` still becomes `dair`.
+- Polkit challenges are now reported as `org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.InteractiveAuthorizationRequired` when the caller passed `interactive=false` but authentication is possible, instead of a generic `AUTH_FAILED`, so GUI clients can retry with an agent dialog (matches localed).
+
+### Added
+- Device-tree fallbacks for platforms without DMI (ARM, RISC-V, e.g. Raspberry Pi): `HardwareModel` from `/sys/firmware/devicetree/base/model`, `HardwareVendor` from the vendor prefix of the first `compatible` entry, and `Chassis` from `chassis-type` when it is a known value.
+- `HardwareVendor` now prefers DMI `sys_vendor`, then `board_vendor` (previously `board_vendor` only), consistent with `hostnamectl`.
+- Expanded chassis table: rack-mount, multi-system and blade types map to `server`; IoT gateway and embedded PC map to `embedded`; all-in-one, pizza-box, space-saving, lunch-box, sealed-case, mini-PC and stick-PC map to `desktop`. The case tables in `slack/hostnamectl` were updated to match.
+
+## [0.2.7.1] - 2026-06-27 to 2026-09-01
+- Added validation for hostname metadata values and corrected the machine-info path constant.
+- Man pages for `hostnamed(8)` and `hostnamectl(1)` added and compressed in the SlackBuild.
+- New and updated translations (Arabic Latin script, Indonesian, Estonian and others) via Weblate; project version bumped to 0.2.7 then 0.2.7.1.
+- Removed `sbindir` paths from the build.
+
 ## [0.2.6] - 2026-06-20
 
 ### Security
